    Receives the text between the outer quote characters, exactly as it
    appears in the input (backslashes still present).

    Must return the decoded string. The decision of how backslash
    sequences are interpreted (which escapes are recognised, what a
    backslash before an ordinary character means, and whether a trailing
    lone backslash is kept or dropped) is left to the implementer.
    """
    raise NotImplementedError


